WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.968
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with John Oliver.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:05.968
I always think about you --

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.868
You've been very critical,
rightfully so,

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.200
of FIFA over the years.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.000
-Yes, because it's basically
a criminal cartel

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.968
that stages a tournament
every four years.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.667
-Yeah, there's a perfect example
of what I was just doing.

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.767
But, you know, a lot of people,
they basically just stepped up

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:24.434
and did as right a thing
as they are likely to do.

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:26.200
-It is kind of amazing.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.934
If you have lost the moral high
ground, as a country, to FIFA...

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:34.434
[ Laughter ]
...you are morally subterranean

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:38.868
because they will try
every possible angle to do

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:41.767
the wrong thing, and if they
couldn't find that

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:44.701
and they ended up kicking them
out, things are bad.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.167
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:50.534
And they did try to do the wrong
version of the right thing.

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:51.801
-That's the best move, saying,

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:54.467
"Yeah, you can compete,
but just not as Russia.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.567
You got to change your names

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.367
and you got to wear
fake mustaches."

00:00:58.367 --> 00:00:59.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:03.334
"That'll teach you, right?
That'll teach you."

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:05.400
-But it's not change your name
to like

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.167
the Grasshoppers,
which would be fun.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.934
It's always like "the Federation
of Russian Athletes."

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.834
-That's right. That's right.
Exactly.

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:15.234
"The team formerly known as
the Russian football team."

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:20.133
But also you just cannot let
FIFA occupy any kind of morality

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:22.934
here because they are banning
Russia from the World Cup

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:25.767
in Qatar...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:28.067
...which is basically
built on blood.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:32.000
So yeah, FIFA,
in the macro sense,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.868
are still continuing to do
the wrong thing

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.634
and will until the end
of their existence.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:38.934
-And yet -- I know this because
we text a lot during

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:41.334
international football --
I'm going to say "football"

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.434
because you're here.
-I appreciate that.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:44.734
-No worries.
I want you to feel comfortable.

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:46.334
I don't want you to be like,
"What?"

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:50.801
[ Laughter ]
-You're a great host, Seth.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:53.033
-How invested will you be
in the World Cup?

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:56.400
-You know, it just gets to
the fundamental flaw

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.567
of you as a human being.

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:59.601
I mean me, but also you.

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:00.767
-Yes, also me, yeah.

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:04.300
-Because you cannot
defend the fact

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.000
the World Cup is happening
in Qatar.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.234
And I am going to watch it.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:09.467
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:13.767
-And I am going to criticize it
before and after.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.734
-Yeah.
-And who knows? During.

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:17.167
-Yeah.

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:18.934
-But I am going to watch it.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.467
And what does that make me?

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:24.133
It's some version of
a kind of lower-H hypocrite.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:28.367
-It is lower H.
-Yeah, lower H, lower H.

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:29.501
It's not capital H.

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:30.834
-No, I would never say that
of you.

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.501
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, there's the thing.

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:34.834
I love the product
they make so much,

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:37.567
just like drug cartels
make a very fine cocaine.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:39.634
[ Laughter ]
-That's very nice of you to say.

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:42.167
Nobody ever says that about
the drug cartels.

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:45.801
Let's not forget that they're
making very good cocaine.

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:49.033
-I cannot say this enough, and
this isn't sponsored content,

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.334
the Sinaloa Cartel...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:55.367
...makes some of,
if not the best, cocaine around.

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:56.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:59.133
If you're not taking
Sinaloa Cocaine --

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:01.534
-I will say, this is starting to
sound like an ad,

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:04.634
but I'm gonna let you finish.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:08.400
It does feel like this is very,
like, written marketing speak.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.400
-I think that is the secret of
lots of late-night shows.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.701
People do often come on
with something to sell.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:18.467
For me, unfortunately, it is the
fact that the Sinaloa Cartel --

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:21.167
[ Laughter ]
Even as I'm doing this bit,

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.334
I'm realizing there are
other cartels

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.033
who might not find this
quite as funny.

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:30.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.267
And that's the prob-- I get too
[bleep] relaxed on this show,

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:36.968
and I either imply that the
coronavirus is not going to be

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:39.734
a big deal in New York, or I
start saying, for some reason,

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.100
that the Sinaloa Cartel --

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.367
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:47.234
What I like to picture right
now, as this airs, is

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:49.868
there's a rival cartel,
and they're having whatever

00:03:49.868 --> 00:03:51.100
kind of meeting they have,

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.534
and there's, like,
two cheetahs and whatnot.

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.000
They're having the meeting.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.334
And there's a TV on in the
corner, and this is on,

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:59.767
and then all of a sudden,
the head of the cartel --

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:02.234
-That's right. And before
this moment's gone on,

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:04.234
they've been talking about,
"Do you think Wally's getting

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:05.501
a little bit too much
screen time?"

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:06.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.067
-And the head of the cartel's
like, "No."

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:09.367
He respects Wally.
-That's right.

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:13.434
-He respects what he's doing.
He wants power.

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:14.767
-He's going to do anything
it takes to get it.

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:17.400
-But right now they're saying,
"Turn it up,"

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.834
because it's on
in the background.

00:04:18.834 --> 00:04:21.467
And now they're going --
-"Hang on, shh, shh. Wait.

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:22.767
The Sinaloa?"

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:28.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.367
-This is very -- We've really
stepped in it, I feel like.

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:31.601
[ Laughter ]
We'll get out of it.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.267
-It'll be fine.
-It'll be fine.

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:34.934
-What's the worst
that can happen?

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:40.267
-Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:43.968
-And that's the gif that people
will use in the future,

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:46.434
when someone gets a little bit
too comfortable about

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.133
something and it blows up
in their face.

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:49.767
"What's the worst
that could happen?"

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:51.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.300
-This is good, though,
because I feel like

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.033
this is erasing our interview
from two years ago.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:56.000
Like now, this is
more interesting.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.100
-You got to keep it fresh.
-Nobody's going to look back.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.734
They're gonna be like,
"They stepped in it freshly."

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:05.033
You actually went,
right after Crimea,

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:07.901
you went to interview Snowden.

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:09.400
-I did.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.200
-Which I imagine was tense
in its own right,

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.400
but even more so
because of the annexation.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:17.067
-It was, actually, and to
the extent that, we got there --

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:19.400
we hadn't told anyone,
our fixer or our crew,

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:20.968
who we were there to interview
because we were keeping it

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:23.467
all very -- See, we hadn't told
HBO either.

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:25.567
So we were keeping it all
very, very --

00:05:25.567 --> 00:05:27.234
-What did HBO think
you were doing?

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:29.667
-They didn't -- They thought --

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:32.434
I think they thought I was in
New York preparing for the show.

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:34.734
-Okay, gotcha.
-Whereas, surprise.

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:38.467
[ Laughter ]
I'm in Russia.

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:41.868
So yeah, we got there,
and it was very, very tense,

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:45.133
and we were clearly,
very obviously being watched.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:48.834
The Russians were not -- There
was no subterfuge going on.

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:50.634
They were very obviously
following us.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:53.367
And our fixer was
really, really worried.

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:55.334
And then when we eventually
said, just before we were

00:05:55.334 --> 00:05:56.968
going to do the interview,
"Actually, it's Snowden,"

00:05:56.968 --> 00:06:00.968
it was immediate relaxation
in the room and from the fixer.

00:06:00.968 --> 00:06:02.901
"Oh, that's okay. That's fine.
You can talk about that.

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:04.601
I thought you were just going to
talk about the other thing."

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:06.734
And then he wouldn't even say
the word.

00:06:06.734 --> 00:06:08.367
-He wouldn't even say "Crimea"?
-He wouldn't even say "Crimea"

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:09.868
because I think he knew that we
were being listened to.

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:12.334
So he just said, "If you're not
talking about the other thing,

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:14.300
this will be okay."
And everything calmed down.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.534
But it was very, very tense.
-I would imagine.

00:06:16.534 --> 00:06:19.767
And then, 2017, you did a piece
about Putin.

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:22.200
-Yes.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:26.133
-I'm assuming -- Do you reach
out, like, for comment?

00:06:26.133 --> 00:06:27.300
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.968
We had a list of questions.

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:31.601
"Vladimir, can you just get back
to us on this?

00:06:31.601 --> 00:06:33.501
Because if you have a response,
we'd love to build the response

00:06:33.501 --> 00:06:36.767
into the body of the script,
if that's okay."

00:06:36.767 --> 00:06:38.467
I can't remember if we --

00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:40.868
Maybe as a courtesy, we reached
out to the Kremlin.

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:42.901
-They respect that.
-That's right.

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:46.267
I do think he would have some
queries with what we said.

00:06:46.267 --> 00:06:49.133
-Yeah.
-No, the only thing we really

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:53.567
did before it went on was really
jack up our cybersecurity.

00:06:53.567 --> 00:06:55.434
-Oh, that's very smart.
-Yeah. Have you done that yet?

00:06:55.434 --> 00:06:57.167
Because the Sinaloa Cartel
may be --

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:58.667
[ Laughter ]
-Are they good at that?

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:01.334
Do they have a good tech guy?
-Seth, I can't say this enough.

00:07:01.334 --> 00:07:03.133
They're good at everything.
-Oh, my God.

00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:06.834
This is a #ad.
John Oliver, everybody.

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:09.300
"Last Week Tonight" airs
Sunday nights on HBO

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.300
and streams on HBO Max.

